  "name": "Flask of royal jelly",
  "description": "A corked flask two-thirds full of jelly, the fill line sitting flat across the glass with air above it. The glass is pale rather than clear: over a dark panel a transparent bottle is no bottle at all, so the walls carry a little white of their own and the jelly reads as being inside something. Polish: the jelly is a dark base under a lit top instead of one flat gold, the cork has a shaded right side and a full-width ink underlay, and the single gloss on the glass is two pixels wide so it survives 1\u00d7. The glass stays at $silent@0.42 \u2014 that is the approved read. Says pass: two-thirds full is a fraction, and the find is more than the flask was built to hold. The cork is off and leaning, the jelly domes over the lip, and one bead is already down the outside of the glass. Past-full is the whole picture.",
